{"name":"Clarke","label":"Athens-Clarke","run":"Tax Commissioner (ex officio sheriff)","page":"https://www.accgov.com/1719/Tax-Sales","schedule":"First Tuesday when scheduled, 10am, Athens-Clarke County Courthouse","excess":"https://accgov.com/3910/Excess-Funds","parcel":"https://qpublic.schneidercorp.com/","note":"No sale on October 6, 2026. The excess funds list includes the winning bid for 2020 to 2025 sales.","auction":{"venue":"In front of the Athens-Clarke County Courthouse","address":"325 E. Washington St., Athens, GA 30601","time":"First Tuesday of the month, beginning at 10:00 am. If parcels remain unsold at 4:00 pm the sale resumes at 10:00 am the next day.","registration":"No advance registration procedure is published. The purchaser must give the Tax Commissioner a current mailing address when tendering payment and receives a receipt.","payment":"Payment for the bid is due at the time of sale, by cashier's or certified check issued or certified by an FDIC or FSLIC insured institution.","phone":"706-613-3120","email":"tc@accgov.com","office":"Athens-Clarke County Tax Commissioner, Delinquent Tax Division","office_address":"325 E. Washington St., Suite 250, Athens, GA 30601 (mailing: P.O. Box 1868, Athens, GA 30603)","vital":["Public outcry auction, usually in the order of the legal ads. The opening bid equals the taxes due plus costs, and the property may be bid in for the county if no one bids above it.","A bidder who fails to pay is liable for any shortfall when the property is resold.","The tax deed is not a warranty deed. The buyer must check title and is responsible for property taxes as they come due.","The owner or any interest holder has 12 months to redeem. The price is the bid plus taxes paid plus a 20% premium for the first year and 10% for each year after.","The buyer must foreclose the right of redemption by notice after one year or fee simple title does not vest.","Excess funds are released only to a claimant or the claimant's Georgia attorn